55. CANONICAL PRINCIPLE

The PRSL-AI Ecosystem must protect not only the user's data, but also the user's ability to control what happens to that data.

==================================================

56. CANONICAL DEFINITION

PRSL-AI Privacy & Security is the cross-cutting architectural capability responsible for protecting user identity, information, context, memory, knowledge, communications, capabilities, devices and actions through privacy-by-default, local-first processing, data minimization, authorization, isolation, encryption, controlled retention and continuous security enforcement.

==================================================

57. FINAL PRINCIPLE

Privacy is not a feature.

Security is not a setting.

Accessibility is not an exception.

Trust is not a request.

The PRSL-AI Ecosystem must earn trust through architecture and behavior.

The user remains the center.

The user's data remains under meaningful control.

And every component of the ecosystem must operate within boundaries designed to protect that relationship.

